The '''Temple of Ikov''' is a dungeon underneath [[Hemenster]]. The main entrance to the dungeon is located south of the [[Ranging Guild]]. The second entrance inside the house in [[McGrubor's Wood]] requires a [[shiny key]].

There are no requirements to access the dungeon, however players that have not completed the [[Temple of Ikov]] quest will need to wear a [[pendant of Lucien]] to pass through the gates north-west of the southern entrance.

{{Map|name=Entrances to Temple of Ikov Dungeon|x:2677,y:3405|x:2659,y:3492|mtype=pin|align=left|caption=The two entrances to the dungeon.}}
The dungeon is also the only place that contains the [[boots of lightness]] (except through [[Perdu]]). Players must bring a [[knife]] or a [[Slash weapons|slash weapon]], as well as a [[Light sources|light source]], and go down the stairs near the entrance of the dungeon. Players must slash the web to collect the boots on the other side of the small room, which will lower weight by 4.535 kg when equipped.

The Temple of Ikov is the site of the only remaining temple of Armadyl in Gielinor, on the other side of the dungeon, and is inhabited by the [[Guardians of Armadyl]]. This is also where the [[Staff of Armadyl]] was located. The guardians serve to protect the Staff of Armadyl, a very powerful staff used by [[Zamorak]] to betray [[Zaros]] and ascend to godhood at the end of the [[Second Age]].

